  "title": "Guo Shoujing",
  "summary": "Guo Shoujing was a Yuan-dynasty astronomer and hydraulic engineer born in Xingtai, Hebei. He designed Kublai Khan's Beijing observatory in 1279, headed it from 1283, and helped compile the calendar adopted in 1281 and used for 364 years. In 1292 he became head of the Water Works Bureau.",
